.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap33/review_prompt1.txt
Review the uncommitted stmap33 iteration in this ABC repository.

Project context:
- This is AutoEDA iteration stmap33 in the stmap mapper family.
- The binding project pack requires preserving older stmap commands, adding a numbered command with -h usage, and validating against build/help/smoke/full benchmark/CEC gates.
- stmap33 should keep prior stmap32 behavior available and add only the new mode 34 behavior for the stmap33 command.

Implementation hypothesis:
- Keep the stmap32 cut-leaf load proxy path, but normalize the strong deep seed penalty by the selected supergate fanout limit.
- The goal is to test a library-derived drive/load signal rather than relying only on raw cut-leaf reference counts.

Files of interest:
- src/base/abci/abc.c
- src/base/abci/abcStmap_33.c
- src/base/abci/module.make
- abclib.dsp
- src/map/mapper/mapperInt.h
- src/map/mapper/mapperCore.c
- src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c
- .autoeda/runtime/results/stmap33/*

Validation already run before this review:
- make ABC_USE_NO_READLINE=1
- ./abc -c "stmap33 -h"
- smoke flow on benchmarks/i10.aig
- baseline and candidate flows on all four required benchmarks
- CEC on all four required benchmarks

Please focus on correctness and campaign-contract risks:
- command registration/build integration
- whether mode 34 is properly gated and does not alter map or stmap0 through stmap32 behavior
- whether the stmap33 penalty/diagnostic counters are internally consistent
- whether any uninitialized values, bad short-circuit assumptions, or parse/logging hazards exist
- whether any required artifacts or validation steps appear missing

Return findings first, ordered by severity, with file/line references where possible. If there are no actionable findings, say so clearly and mention residual risk.
