   714	/**Function*************************************************************
   715	
   716	  Synopsis    [Returns 1 if a fanout/load proxy should reject this cut.]
   717	
   718	  Description [Mode 1 is the classic map -f guard. Mode 2 is the stmap1
   719	  selective guard, which only rejects wider cuts when the node has higher
   720	  estimated fanout. Mode 3 is the stmap2 guard, which uses the same fanout
   721	  thresholds only during area recovery and only when the current phase has
   722	  slack over the mapper required time. Mode 4 is the stmap3 guard, which
   723	  narrows the intervention to high-fanout nodes with only shallow positive
   724	  slack. Mode 5 is the stmap4 split-phase guard: stmap1-style guarding in
   725	  delay matching and stmap2-style slack-aware guarding in area recovery.
   726	  Mode 6 is the stmap5 shape-gated split-phase guard: the delay pass only
   727	  uses stmap1-style guarding in very large mapper graphs, while area recovery
   728	  keeps the stmap2 slack-aware guard. Mode 7 is the stmap6 area-sensitive
   729	  shape-gated guard: the delay pass keeps the stmap5 graph-size gate, small
   730	  mapper graphs keep the stmap2 slack-aware recovery guard, and exact-area
   731	  recovery on larger graphs checks the cut after matching so materially cheaper
   732	  cuts can override the fanout/load proxy. Mode 8 is the stmap7 criticality-
   733	  sensitive version of mode 7: exact-area recovery on larger graphs allows the
   734	  override only with deeper mapper slack and outside the highest fanout bucket.
   735	  Mode 9 is the stmap8 arrival-bounded version of mode 8: the area-saving
   736	  override also requires the candidate match to stay within one quarter of an
   737	  inverter delay of the existing mapper arrival. Mode 10 is the stmap9
   738	  middle-slack area-relief version of mode 9: it keeps the highest fanout
   739	  bucket protected, but in the one-to-two inverter slack bucket it allows a
   740	  wide cut only when it is arrival-neutral and saves at least one inverter
   741	  area. Mode 11 is the stmap10 depth-qualified version of mode 10: the
   742	  middle-slack relief is allowed only for shallow and medium-depth nodes.
   743	  Mode 12 is the stmap11 tight-depth version of mode 11: the middle-slack
   744	  relief is allowed only for shallower nodes. Mode 13 is the stmap12
   745	  fanout-bucket split version of mode 12: the tight-depth middle-slack relief
   746	  is allowed only in the lower moderate fanout bucket. Mode 14 is stmap13,
   747	  which keeps mode 13 behavior while recording guard-hit counters. Mode 15 is
   748	  stmap14, which keeps the same bucket and counters but requires a stronger
   749	  middle-slack area-flow saving. Mode 16 is stmap15, which restores the
   750	  one-inverter relief threshold only after the current run has observed a high
   751	  lower-moderate/middle-slack exact-area profile. Mode 17 is stmap16, which
   752	  keeps mode 16 behavior and prints per-relief diagnostics. Mode 18 is stmap17,
   753	  which uses the one-inverter post-profile threshold only for candidates with
   754	  materially better mapper arrival. Mode 19 is stmap18, which keeps mode 18
   755	  decisions and adds near-miss diagnostics for candidates rejected by the
   756	  timing-quality/profile fallback. Mode 20 is stmap19, which allows the
   757	  one-inverter threshold before profile-open only for candidates with the same
   758	  material mapper-arrival improvement. Mode 21 is stmap20, which keeps the
   759	  mode 20 pre-profile seed but restricts it to shallow nodes. Mode 22 is
   760	  stmap21, which keeps the shallow seed and admits deeper pre-profile seeds
   960	  candidate match worsens mapper arrival by more than one quarter of an
   961	  inverter delay. In stmap9, middle-slack candidates can recover area only
   962	  when they are outside the highest fanout bucket, do not worsen mapper
   963	  arrival, and save at least one inverter area. In stmap10, that middle-slack
   964	  relief also requires the mapper node to be no deeper than level 96. In
   965	  stmap11, that depth window is tightened to level 64. In stmap12, the same
   966	  tight-depth relief is allowed only in the lower moderate fanout bucket. In
   967	  stmap13, the same decision path also records exact-area guard statistics. In
   968	  stmap14, the lower-moderate middle-slack relief must save two inverter areas
   969	  instead of one. In stmap15, one-inverter relief is restored only after the
   970	  mapper observes a high lower-moderate/middle-slack profile. In stmap16, the
   971	  same behavior also reports each admitted relief choice. In stmap17, the
   972	  adaptive one-inverter relief threshold also requires a material mapper-arrival
   973	  improvement; arrival-neutral choices keep the stricter two-inverter fallback.
   974	  In stmap18, the same decisions are preserved while near-miss rejected
   975	  middle-slack candidates are logged. In stmap19, pre-profile one-inverter
   976	  relief is seeded only by candidates with the same material arrival gain. In
   977	  stmap20, the pre-profile seed is further limited to shallow nodes. In
   978	  stmap21, deeper pre-profile seeds are allowed only with a much larger mapper
   979	  arrival gain. In stmap22, the same deep-seed path is relaxed to a moderate
   980	  mapper-arrival gain. In stmap23, moderate deep seeds also need near-critical
   981	  existing mapper slack. In stmap24, the moderate deep slack gate is tightened
   982	  to the lower edge of the critical slack window. In stmap25, the stmap24 rule
   983	  is kept, and one moderate deep seed from the next slack band is admitted for
   984	  ablation. In stmap26, the first such moderate seed is skipped and only the
   985	  second qualifying seed is admitted. In stmap27, moderate deep candidates in
